From: ascend-torchtitan <maintainers@ascend-torchtitan>
Subject: [PATCH] TORCH-7: opcheck: allow privateuse1 devices in autograd_registration_check

Problem: torch.library.opcheck's autograd registration check rejects any
device outside CPU/CUDA/XPU ("NYI devices other than CPU/CUDA/XPU, got
{'npu'}"), so custom ops for out-of-tree backends cannot be validated with
opcheck even though the check is device-agnostic.

Fix: accept the registered privateuse1 backend name and probe
AutogradPrivateUse1.

Baseline: torch 2.13.0 (same code in 2.12.0 and nightly 2.15.0.dev20260828).
Validation: ascend-torchtitan tests/npu/test_kernel_attention.py opcheck with
test_autograd_registration enabled on Ascend (torch_npu registers its custom
op autograd under AutogradPrivateUse1).
---
--- a/torch/testing/_internal/optests/autograd_registration.py	2026-07-03 22:18:38.000000000 +0800
+++ b/torch/testing/_internal/optests/autograd_registration.py	2026-08-29 23:36:04.970210460 +0800
@@ -84,13 +84,19 @@
 
     # Determine which AutogradBACKEND key to check
     all_device_types = {arg.device.type for arg in all_tensors}
-    if not all_device_types.issubset(["cpu", "cuda", "xpu"]):
+    privateuse1 = torch._C._get_privateuse1_backend_name()
+    if not all_device_types.issubset(["cpu", "cuda", "xpu", privateuse1]):
         # Don't want to support other keys yet
         raise NotImplementedError(
-            f"autograd_registration_check: NYI devices other than CPU/CUDA/XPU, got {all_device_types}"
+            f"autograd_registration_check: NYI devices other than CPU/CUDA/XPU/{privateuse1}, "
+            f"got {all_device_types}"
         )
     if "cuda" in all_device_types:
         key = "AutogradCUDA"
+    elif privateuse1 in all_device_types:
+        # Out-of-tree backends (e.g. torch_npu) register their autograd kernels
+        # under AutogradPrivateUse1; the check itself is device-agnostic.
+        key = "AutogradPrivateUse1"
     elif "cpu" in all_device_types:
         key = "AutogradCPU"
     elif "xpu" in all_device_types:
